<title>UK: Chrysalis sells outside broadcast business.</title>
<headline>Chrysalis sells outside broadcast business.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British media company Chrysalis Group Plc said on Friday said it has sold its subsidiary Chrysalis Television Mobiles Ltd (CTM) to two private companies owned by the founder of CTM.</p>
<p>CTM was the group's last outside broadcast business and was originally bought from founder Malcolm Bartram and his associates in 1987.</p>
<p>Bartram is paying around 2.95 million stg for the business.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
